{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"id\":\"N01\",\"lines\":\"nr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N01.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"مَٰلِكِ\",\"target_ar\":\"يَوْمِ\",\"after\":\"The owned Day briefly carries the image of a marriage occasion.\",\"reason\":\"إملاك and التزويج name a marriage ceremony, while يَوْمِ is a span or event-day. A ceremony has a time, but that link is generic.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N01.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"مَٰلِكِ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلدِّينِ\",\"after\":\"Marriage covenant and debt are both binding claims. Heard together, the Day becomes the horizon on which even covenantal obligations are answered.\",\"reason\":\"إملاك/التزويج is a marriage contract; دِين can name debt, obligation, and repayment. The pair links a binding covenant with the account of obligations.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N02\",\"lines\":\"-n\"}\n{\"id\":\"N02.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"مَٰلِكِ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلدِّينِ\",\"after\":\"The order can feel like a path with a central course, though the link is broad.\",\"reason\":\"مَلَك الطريق is its وسطه or معظمه, its middle or main stretch; دِين names obedience and an order of belief. The center is part of a path, an indirect link to dīn as an ordered way.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N03\",\"lines\":\"nn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N03.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"مَٰلِكِ\",\"target_ar\":\"يَوْمِ\",\"after\":\"It briefly evokes water as a traveler's provision through a day.\",\"reason\":\"الماء ملك أمره is water that sustains a traveler's affairs; يَوْمِ is a temporal span or event-day. Provision and the span it carries someone through are complementary, but broadly so.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N03.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"مَٰلِكِ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلدِّينِ\",\"after\":\"It hints that the order defining the Day rests on life's sustaining provision.\",\"reason\":\"الماء ملاك الأشياء is water as what sustains or completes affairs; دِين is an order of obedience and conduct. Material sustenance can support such an order, a broad part relation.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N04\",\"lines\":\"-r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N04.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"مَٰلِكِ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلدِّينِ\",\"after\":\"The Day becomes a scene of following the one who leads. It brings obedience into the image of a guide moving ahead of those behind him.\",\"reason\":\"مَلَك الدابة can mean its guide or leading element; دِين means الطاعة والانقياد, obedience and submission. The guide and those who follow form complementary roles.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N05\",\"lines\":\"rn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N05.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"يَوْمِ\",\"target_ar\":\"مَٰلِكِ\",\"after\":\"A bounded daylight span is heard as something fully possessed and governed. This sharpens the reach of the sovereign's authority over the Day.\",\"reason\":\"يَوْمِ can mean the daylight from sunrise to sunset; مَٰلِكِ carries ownership and disposal. The finite time-span and its owner form a direct complement.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N05.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"يَوْمِ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلدِّينِ\",\"after\":\"The solar day offers a familiar time-frame for the reckoning.\",\"reason\":\"يَوْمِ can mean the bounded daylight span; دِين names judgment and requital. Time-frame and reckoning complement each other, though the solar limit is not specified for the Judgment Day.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N06\",\"lines\":\"rr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N06.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلدِّينِ\",\"target_ar\":\"مَٰلِكِ\",\"after\":\"Ownership and enforced subjection become two faces of dominion. The Day belongs to the one who can bring its subjects low.\",\"reason\":\"دَانَهُ can mean to humble or enslave someone; مَٰلِكِ names ownership and power to dispose. Both senses meet in coercive mastery, from the ruler's side and the subject's.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N06.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلدِّينِ\",\"target_ar\":\"يَوْمِ\",\"after\":\"The Day becomes a scene of abasement before the sovereign. Its severity is heard as the subjection of those brought low.\",\"reason\":\"دَانَهُ means to humble or enslave; يَوْمِ can name a great and severe event. Together they picture a momentous Day marked by humiliation and subjection.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N07\",\"lines\":\"rr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N07.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلدِّينِ\",\"target_ar\":\"مَٰلِكِ\",\"after\":\"The possessor's authority is heard as a support fit to be trusted with judgment. The pair makes the Day's ownership a charge entrusted to its disposer.\",\"reason\":\"دَيَّنْتُ الرجل can mean to credit him in court or entrust him to his own دِين; مِلاك الأمر is the support that sustains an affair, and مَٰلِكِ names its disposer. Entrustment and responsible authority complement each other.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N07.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلدِّينِ\",\"target_ar\":\"يَوْمِ\",\"after\":\"The Day becomes the occasion when each person answers for their avowed word and creed. The rare judicial sense gives the event a scene of personal evaluation.\",\"reason\":\"دَيَّنْتُ الرجل can mean to evaluate or credit him in court, while يَوْمِ is a bounded, momentous event-day. The judicial assessment and its appointed time complete one another.\"}"}}
